!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/two-definition-marks-on-one-declaration-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §12.1"
  description: """
    The three ways a record may be realised are alternatives, so the grammar gives them one optional
    slot rather than two independent flags: ABSTRACT has no instances of its own and FINAL has instances
    and no subtype, and a record claiming both would have no values anywhere. Writing two is therefore
    ungrammatical, not a rule a resolver has to state and check -- which is the observable difference
    between one slot and two.

    Category is `resolver` even though the failure is a parse one: §8.1 makes every error that stops a
    schema loading a resolver error, however early the phase that caught it.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
